    [BugFix][KV Pool] Skip probes for HBM-cached prefixes (#19755)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Layerwise hit checks probe pooled blocks even when their prefix is
    already resident in local HBM. With Memcache, a readability query can
    synchronously rewarm SSD data or wait for pending rewarm, delaying
    EngineCore scheduling despite providing no additional external hit
    tokens.
    
    Pass the local hit length into the hybrid coordinator and filter
    complete local group blocks before constructing backend query keys.
    Reuse the coordinator's existing HBM hit accounting and apply the same
    offset to contiguous lookup. Keep partial group blocks and
    layer-reuse/offload probing intact.
    
    Main counterpart of #19754 (`releases/v0.30.0`).
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Layerwise lookup avoids redundant pool probes and their rewarm side
    effects for complete, locally resident prefixes. No new configuration or
    SDK flag changes. This does not change Meta's pending-rewarm cleanup
    behavior.
    
    Release note: `release_notes/fragments/19755.yaml`.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - The release counterpart passed **866 CPU tests, 12 skipped** with
    `python3 -m pytest -q -rs tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store`. This is
    supporting release-branch evidence, not a main-branch pass claim.
    - Five added regression tests cover zero backend calls for fully local
    prefixes, partial local prefixes with pooled tail extension, missing
    pooled tails retaining local hits, different group block sizes, and
    preserved layer-reuse behavior.
    - Ruff 0.14.0 lint/format checks on both changed main files and `git
    diff --check` passed.
    - Main's normal test command could not collect: the development
    container's vLLM lacks `vllm.v1.core.kv_cache_planning`. An isolated
    directory-only attempt also encountered dependency initialization
    errors; no main runtime test pass is claimed.
    - GitHub's full `pre-commit` check passed on
    `97da698f6b4f13802bb14c97a9d42273a8cda1f8`; DCO also passed. `bash
    format.sh ci` also passed locally on the ARM64 development host for this
    branch (exit 0, all hooks passed), using the supplied proxy and
    architecture-correct lint tools; `git diff --check` passed.
    - NPU correctness, end-to-end behavior and a before/after performance
    benchmark remain for CI/hardware validation; no measured prefill speedup
    is claimed.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    - [x] Boundary / edge-case coverage: complete/partial local hits and
    different group block sizes.
    - [x] Regression tests exercise backend query key sets and returned hit
    lengths.
    - [x] Missing-pool-tail behavior is covered.
    - [ ] Main-compatible runtime tests and NPU/performance validation.
    - [x] Full repository format hooks passed in GitHub CI.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
